# Local HTTPS / HTTP-2 terminator for the whole dev stack.
#
# The https ports here are the BROWSER-FACING origins. The Vite dev servers and the API stay
# on plain http behind this proxy and shouldn't be opened directly.
#
#   https://localhost:3443  ->  :3005  api (Hono)
#   https://localhost:3444  ->  :3001  central
#   https://localhost:3445  ->  :3003  hr
#   https://localhost:3446  ->  :3004  admin
#   https://localhost:3447  ->  :3006  website-management
#   https://localhost:3448  ->  :3007  public
#
# Why HTTPS for everything, not just the API:
#
# 1. HTTP/2. Every ElectricSQL shape holds a long-poll against the API origin. Over HTTP/1.1
#    the browser caps one origin at ~6 concurrent connections, so a page holding several live
#    shapes starves and dev feels frozen (Electric logs a warning about this). TLS here gives
#    the browser HTTP/2 multiplexing — effectively unlimited concurrent shape streams.
#    Ref: https://electric.ax/docs/sync/guides/troubleshooting
#
# 2. Cookies. Fronting ONLY the API is actively broken: an http:// page calling an https://
#    API is *cross-site* under Chrome's schemeful same-site rules, so the SameSite=Lax session
#    cookie is withheld and the app bounces back to /login forever. Page and API have to share
#    a scheme. Serving both over https satisfies that and gets HTTP/2 at the same time.
#
# Usage (run Caddy on the host — NOT in Docker; containers break HTTP/2):
#   caddy trust            # one-time: trust Caddy's local CA (needs admin / UAC)
#   caddy run              # auto-loads this Caddyfile from the repo root
#
# Each upstream keeps its own Host header so Vite's host checks and Better Auth's
# BETTER_AUTH_URL (http://localhost:3005) still match, and the session cookie stays host-only
# on `localhost` — shared across every localhost port, which is what gives us dev SSO.
#
# Ports: 3443-3448 and the admin endpoint on 2020 deliberately avoid 3000, 3002, 5173-5176,
# 80 and 2019, which a concurrent project on this machine reserves (see CLAUDE.md).

# Move the admin endpoint off the default :2019 so this instance can coexist with another
# Caddy already running, and skip the automatic HTTP->HTTPS redirect listener (it would try to
# bind :80, already taken on Windows by http.sys / the other Caddy).
{
	admin localhost:2020
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

https://localhost:3443 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3005 {
		header_up Host localhost:3005
	}
}

# The app servers. reverse_proxy upgrades WebSockets automatically, which is what carries
# Vite's HMR socket — each app's vite config points its HMR client at the port below.
https://localhost:3444 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3001 {
		header_up Host localhost:3001
	}
}

https://localhost:3445 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3003 {
		header_up Host localhost:3003
	}
}

https://localhost:3446 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3004 {
		header_up Host localhost:3004
	}
}

https://localhost:3447 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3006 {
		header_up Host localhost:3006
	}
}

https://localhost:3448 {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3007 {
		header_up Host localhost:3007
	}
}
